{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773432592,"nonce":"fcxdh1i03PmVGl8L4X4rpDBa5v4=","title":"push-sync: support non-YubiKey auth methods (1Password SSH, Touch ID, ssh-agent)","message":"Currently push_ssh_identity assumes a hardware key (YubiKey SK key). Users without a YubiKey should be able to use:\n\n1. **1Password SSH agent** - 1Password can act as an SSH agent and uses biometric (Touch ID on Mac) or pin for auth. Works via SSH_AUTH_SOCK pointing to the 1Password agent socket. In this case, the pre-auth ControlMaster approach should still work - the first SSH connection triggers the biometric prompt, subsequent ones reuse the socket.\n\n2. **Touch ID / platform authenticator** - macOS Sequoia supports ed25519-sk keys backed by the Secure Enclave. These behave like YubiKey SK keys but use fingerprint instead of hardware touch.\n\n3. **Plain ssh-agent** - User may have a non-SK key loaded in ssh-agent that they consider adequate for push auth. In this case, they should be able to opt into the pre-auth flow without specifying an identity file (just use whatever the agent offers).\n\n4. **No extra auth** - Some users may have passwordless keys or already-unlocked agents and just want the ControlMaster connection reuse for speed, not security gating.\n\nProposal: make push_ssh_identity optional but add a push_ssh_preauth setting:\n- \"none\" = no pre-auth, no IdentitiesOnly (current old behavior, effectively)\n- \"agent\" = pre-auth using whatever is in ssh-agent (ControlMaster reuse for speed; no key restriction)\n- \"identity:\u003cpath\u003e\" = pre-auth using specific identity file with IdentitiesOnly=yes (current new behavior)\n\nThe Settings UI should expose this as a dropdown or radio group with clear descriptions of what each mode means. The \"Touch your YubiKey\" banner text should also adapt based on the configured mode (e.g. \"Authenticating with 1Password...\" or \"Touch your security key...\").\n\nRelated: the pre-auth timeout (currently 120s) may be too long for some setups and too short for others - consider making it configurable.","files":null}]}